WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.120
A school playground in London.

2
00:00:02.170 --> 00:00:05.060
Someone finishes a sentence with: innit.

3
00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:08.370
On the bus home, a greeting: wagwan.

4
00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:11.980
Then a story, told with: this is me.

5
00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:13.320
Picked up online?

6
00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:15.470
Invented in one playground?

7
00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:17.310
Where did all this come from?

8
00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:21.560
In this mission, you'll see why teenagers
so often lead the way when a language

9
00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:22.590
changes.

10
00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:26.250
You'll visit a Detroit high school, and
ask what the students' way of speaking

11
00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:27.380
was signalling.

12
00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:30.850
And you'll follow researchers
who recorded London teenagers,

13
00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:33.430
to find out where their speech came from.

14
00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:37.730
Your mission: find out where
'innit' and 'wagwan' came from.
